  "body": "This proposal is a kind of companion proposal to the [number/measurement/quantity tag](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9294) proposal.\r\n\r\nAdd an attribute to the time html tag.  Possible names:\r\n\r\n1.  deriveText\r\n2.  deriveTextFromDateTime\r\n3.  contentFromDateTime\r\n\r\nor some other similar name.  This would ensure backwards compatibility.\r\n\r\nWith the presence of such an attribute, we could add all the properties that [intl.DateTimeFormat](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/DateTimeFormat) supports, e.g.:\r\n\r\n1.  lang (already supported global attribute).\r\n2.  dateStyle\r\n3.  timeStyle\r\n4.  timeZone\r\n\r\netc.\r\n\r\nIf none of these are provided, maybe just set the text based on toLocaleDateString().",
